# Supabase project settings > API.
#
# NAMES MATTER. This is a Vite app, and Vite only exposes variables prefixed
# VITE_ to the browser bundle. Supabase's dashboard shows a Next.js snippet
# using NEXT_PUBLIC_ names — copying that verbatim leaves both values
# undefined here and the app shows the setup screen as though no keys existed.
#
# Either key format works for the second value: the legacy anon JWT that
# starts `eyJ...`, or the newer publishable key that starts `sb_publishable_`.
#
# Both values are safe in a browser bundle: they grant exactly what the RLS
# policies in supabase/migrations/0002 allow, and after 0005 the signed-out
# role cannot reach the tables at all.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-OR-PUBLISHABLE-KEY
